# KNOWN GAP — `Box[enum]` with a resource-carrying variant: the C lane REFUSES
# TO COMPILE and the LLVM lane compiles then DOUBLE-FREES. A Core #9 lane
# divergence AND a Core #8 >=2-bug row.
#
#     Box[V] b = Box(s.v)          # s.v is a field, i.e. a Ptr-typed source
#
#     C    lane: build rc 1, `error: unknown type name 'Box__V'`
#     LLVM lane: build rc 0, run rc 134, `free(): double free detected`
#
# Neither lane is correct, so "the backends disagree" understates it: this is
# >=2 bugs (Core #8), not one lane's problem. The C side never emits the
# `Box__V` struct at all; the LLVM side emits it and then drops the payload
# twice.
#
# ⚠ The LLVM side is NOT "correct but divergent". An earlier reading recorded
# LLVM as running correctly here; with a RESOURCE-carrying variant (the shape
# below) it double-frees. A non-resource variant would be a false negative --
# keep the String payload.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints 1, on BOTH backends.
# Measured 2026-08-27 at HEAD; orchestrator-verified on both lanes.

enum V:
    A(String)
    B(int)

struct S:
    V v

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    S s = S(V.A(mk("aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "bbbbbbbb")))
    Box[V] b = Box(s.v)
    print(1)
